{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chardet/chardet/issues/comments/4098524555","html_url":"https://github.com/chardet/chardet/issues/334#issuecomment-4098524555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chardet/chardet/issues/334","id":4098524555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAE9Mqc70SoWL","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?u=9f230785f700f24a0349413d12389fdb1a89e9d6&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-20T14:42:42Z","updated_at":"2026-03-20T14:42:42Z","author_association":"NONE","body":"I did not intend for this issue to rehash condemnation of @dan-blanchard over the non-use of LGPL but rather to assume the non-use of LGPL is legitimate (in a legal sense, obviously socio-cultural criticisms are very valid) and address the appropriateness of using the MIT or indeed *any* license for AI-generated code, which is a completely different topic. @dan-blanchard I think you understand the issue I'm raising so you might be justified in closing this issue if you want to. \n\nFWIW, IANDBL, TINLA, etc., I don't currently see any basis for concluding that chardet 7.0.0 is required to be released under the LGPL. AFAIK no one including Mark Pilgrim has identified persistence of copyrightable expressive material from earlier versions in 7.0.0 nor has anyone articulated some viable alternate theory of license violation. I don't think I personally would have used the MIT license here, even if I somehow rewrote everything from scratch without the use of AI in a way that didn't implicate obligations flowing from earlier versions of chardet, but that's irrelevant. ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/chardet/chardet/issues/comments/4098524555/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":{"pinned_by":{"login":"dan-blanchard","id":976345,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NjM0NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/976345?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard","html_url":"https://github.com/dan-blanchard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-blanchard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"pinned_at":"2026-03-26T04:29:02Z"}}